  "verbalization": "The evidence suggests a potential relationship between Ceftriaxone and Slc22a11, mediated through the organic anion transport system. Ceftriaxone, a cephalosporin antibiotic, is included in the broader class of cephalosporins, which includes cefotaxime and cefoperazone. These antibiotics bind to Slc22a11, a member of the Slc22 family of transporters, which is involved in the transport of organic anions. This pathway is supported by multiple paths, all of which indicate that Ceftriaxone interacts with Slc22a11 through a common ancestor in the cephalosporin class. The low scores in Path 3, which indicates a weaker direct interaction, may reflect the indirect nature of the relationship, as Ceftriaxone binds to Slc22a6, which in turn participates in the transport of organic anions, ultimately involving Slc22a11. The evidence highlights a mechanistic link between Ceftriaxone and Slc22a11, emphasizing the role of transporters in drug action and the importance of the Slc22 family in mediating drug transport.",
